  <section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">01 / The useful differences</p><h2>Apollo vs ZoomInfo<br>at a glance.</h2><p>Both help B2B sales teams find companies and contacts. Your choice comes down to the data, the work you need done and the full cost.</p></div>
    <div class="sg-table-wrap"><table class="lp-table sg-table az-compare" role="table"><caption>Apollo and ZoomInfo: fit, price visibility, phone data and buying risks</caption><thead><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Buying question</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Apollo</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">ZoomInfo</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in guide.comparison %}<tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">{{ row[0] }}</th><td role="cell" data-label="Apollo">{{ row[1] }}</td><td role="cell" data-label="ZoomInfo">{{ row[2] }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="az-verdict-pair"><article id="apollo"><h3>Apollo: a sensible starting point.</h3><p>Apollo combines contact search, sequences and calling at a published price, which makes it easier to budget for a small team.</p><p><strong>Watch the credits:</strong> phone reveals and other actions use them up, so the allowance can disappear faster than you expect.</p></article><article id="zoominfo"><h3>ZoomInfo: make the package earn its price.</h3><p>Organisation charts and account signals can help you find the right people in a complex buying process.</p><p><strong>No public price:</strong> you have to request a quote before you can compare the cost of the sales platform.</p></article></div>
    <p class="az-inline-sources">Sources: <a href="https://www.apollo.io/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apollo plans ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.zoominfo.com/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ZoomInfo packages ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.zoominfo.com/features/contact-company-search" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ZoomInfo account research ↗</a></p>
  </div></section>

