  <section class="lp-section" id="phone-data"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">03 / Buy numbers you can use</p><h2>Apollo vs ZoomInfo phone data:<br>who can you actually reach?</h2><p>Compare both providers against the companies, roles and territory you actually sell to.</p></div>
    <div class="sg-two"><div><h3>Separate the three calling routes.</h3><ul class="az-numbers"><li><strong>Mobile</strong>A mobile can reach someone away from their desk, though voicemail, call screening and personal-phone objections are common challenges.</li><li><strong>Direct work number</strong>A work line or extension may work best during the buyer's office hours.</li><li><strong>Company number</strong>Reception or a switchboard can help when a direct number is missing or you need to find who handles the decision.</li></ul><p class="sg-sources">Use our <a href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/#call-next">mobile vs company number guide</a> to choose the next call.</p></div><div><h3>Check what “verified” covers.</h3><p>Ask when and how the provider checked the number. A format check tells you less than confirming the person who answers.</p><p>Apollo does not refund mobile credits, so test its mobile results before buying a larger allowance. Office-number and email rules differ.</p><p>ZoomInfo lists mobiles and direct dials alongside company research and contact updates. Those features can help you locate the buyer; the sample still has to show useful coverage.</p><p class="sg-sources"><a href="https://knowledge.apollo.io/hc/en-us/articles/4738396786701-Request-Contact-Data-in-Apollo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apollo data requests and refunds ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.zoominfo.com/features/contact-company-search" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ZoomInfo contact data ↗</a></p></div></div>
    <div class="lp-note"><strong>Use the same 25 target contacts.</strong><p>Count useful mobiles and direct lines, missing records, wrong people and outdated jobs. Keep unanswered calls separate. Check each shared contact once and record which sources supplied it.</p><p><a href="/resources/apollo-alternatives/#contact-test">Copy our 25-contact test →</a></p></div>
    <div class="sg-mid-cta"><p><strong>Have the list but need someone to work it?</strong> Hire CallTeam to prepare the records, make the calls and follow up with the right people.</p><a class="lp-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-booking-placement="apollo-zoominfo-data">Talk to CallTeam ↗</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="credits"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">04 / Follow the contact</p><h2>Credits and export limits:<br>what costs extra?</h2><p>Price the steps from finding someone to putting their number in your calling list.</p></div>
    <div class="sg-table-wrap"><table class="lp-table sg-table az-compare" role="table"><caption>What to check when moving a prospect from search to outreach</caption><thead><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Step</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Apollo</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">ZoomInfo</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Find the buyer</th><td role="cell" data-label="Apollo">Search filters and plan limits shape the list you can select.</td><td role="cell" data-label="ZoomInfo">Check which filters, account signals and research features your package includes.</td></tr>
      <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Get the contact details</th><td role="cell" data-label="Apollo">Published rates: 1 credit for an email and 8 for a phone number. Other enrichment routes can charge differently.</td><td role="cell" data-label="ZoomInfo">Confirm the phone fields included and the allowance for the records you need.</td></tr>
      <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Export to your CRM</th><td role="cell" data-label="Apollo">Export credits apply to some plans or older setups. Check the charge for your account.</td><td role="cell" data-label="ZoomInfo">The pricing FAQ describes 1 credit per exported contact or company profile. Get your package's export rules in writing.</td></tr>
      <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Make the call</th><td role="cell" data-label="Apollo">On credit-based dialling, connected calls use credits, including voicemail. Ring-outs, busy and failed calls use none.</td><td role="cell" data-label="ZoomInfo">Include any required engagement software, dialler, numbers and call usage in the quote.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p class="sg-sources"><a href="https://www.apollo.io/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apollo action rates ↗</a> · <a href="https://knowledge.apollo.io/hc/en-us/articles/9527776320781-Review-Credit-Usage-in-Apollo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apollo export and call charges ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.zoominfo.com/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ZoomInfo export-credit FAQ ↗</a></p>
    <div class="az-credit-example"><h3>1,000 phone reveals can use 8,000 Apollo credits.</h3><p>That covers successful phone reveals at 8 credits each, before email, enrichment or calling.</p></div>
    <div class="sg-two sg-after"><div><h3>ZoomInfo's public wording needs clarity.</h3><p>ZoomInfo promotes platform access without per-credit constraints, but its pricing FAQ describes export credits. The public pages leave buyers to work out which rules apply.</p><p>Get the export allowance, extra-credit price and repeat-export rules alongside the platform fee in your quote.</p><p class="sg-sources"><a href="https://www.zoominfo.com/products/sales" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ZoomInfo's sales-page FAQ ↗</a></p></div><div><h3>Do you already pay for the rest?</h3><p>Your CRM may already handle sequences, call notes and follow-up. Compare those features before buying them again in a data package.</p><p>Check our <a href="/resources/best-crm-for-outbound-sales/">outbound CRM comparison</a>, <a href="/resources/best-cold-calling-dialers/">cold calling dialler prices</a> and <a href="/resources/best-cold-email-software/">cold email software guide</a> for any gaps.</p></div></div>
  </div></section>

